  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+y))-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y}-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(\\frac{1}{2},0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y})}_{(1/2,0)} & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2}+0)}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
